  concept: An LED is a light-emitting diode. It normally emits light when forward
    biased and supplied with appropriate current.
  analogy: Think of an LED as a one-way electrical device that produces light when
    current flows in its intended direction.
  diagram: "Supply + \u2192 Current limiter \u2192 LED anode \u2192 LED cathode \u2192
    Supply \u2212"
  misconception: An LED cannot safely be connected to an arbitrary power source without
    considering polarity, forward voltage and current limiting.
